    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15366" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ējūrātĭo</span></b> 
		(ējĕrātio, <i><span class="en">Tert.
			Spect. 4</span></i>; cf. ejuro), ōnis, f.
		ejuro, II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an abjuring</i>, i. e. <i>a
			resigning</i>, <i>abdication</i>, <i>laying down</i> of an office (post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ignominiosa consulum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 2, 7, 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>a resigning</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bonae spei,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Vit. Beat. 26, 5</span></i>
			.</div>
